export interface Chapter { id: string; kicker: string; title: string; text: string; audio: string; }
export const CHAPTERS: Chapter[] = [{"id": "ch1", "kicker": "Chapter 1", "title": "A real trade", "text": "September second, 2025. QQQ opens down. Most people see a red day. Our system sees a checklist. Five entry gates, momentum, trend, volatility, regime, and machine confidence. That morning, every one of them turned green at once. So the strategy did what it was built to do: buy a deep in-the-money LEAPS call. The QQQ four-sixty-five strike, expiring September 2026. Filled at one thirty-three fifty, the real mid-price, from the real exchange tape. This trade sits inside the five-and-a-half-year record you are about to hear, and it belongs to the final fifteen months, the part we verified tick by tick against the tape.", "audio": "/audio/landing/ch1.mp3"},  {"id": "compound", "kicker": "Chapter 2", "title": "What patience looked like", "text": "Before the mechanics, here is the point. Ten thousand dollars in this strategy became fifty-six thousand, four hundred over five and a half years. The same money in QQQ became twenty-three thousand, six hundred. That is thirty-six point three percent a year against sixteen point six, more than double. And here is why that gap exists. When the twenty twenty-two bear market hit, simply holding QQQ meant sitting in a hole for almost twenty-five months before getting back to even. This strategy sat in cash, then re-entered. Its worst hole of the five years, seventeen point eight percent, recovered in ten weeks. This is not a trading system you babysit. It is a long-term investment that acts only when its rules say act, and otherwise, it waits. The most valuable decision in five years was doing nothing for twelve months while the market fell.", "audio": "/audio/landing/compound.mp3"}, {"id": "ch2", "kicker": "Chapter 3", "title": "The engine", "text": "A LEAPS call is a long-dated option. This one controls a hundred shares of QQQ for over a year, at a fraction of the share price. Deep in the money, it moves nearly dollar-for-dollar with the index. That is the engine: leveraged exposure to QQQ, with a defined cost and no margin. But leverage cuts both ways. When QQQ falls, this position falls faster. You will see exactly that in a moment.", "audio": "/audio/landing/ch2.mp3"}, {"id": "ch3", "kicker": "Chapter 4", "title": "The overlay", "text": "While the LEAPS sits, the strategy sells short-dated calls against it, harvesting premium week after week. Over five and a half years, three hundred ninety-two of these trades. Eighty-five percent of them won, adding thirty-two thousand, nine hundred forty-five dollars, net. But the record also taught us when not to sell. In strong trends with thin premium, the overlay gave back its gains, selling insurance right before the storm. So we tested a rule, in public: strong trend, thin premium, no sale. It cleared our evidence bar across twenty-one out-of-sample tests, and it runs live today. One honest footnote: in the final fifteen months, the tape-verified part, the overlay still lost eighteen hundred dollars net. Win rate is not the same as making money. Every one of those losses is in the ledger.", "audio": "/audio/landing/ch3.mp3"}, {"id": "map", "kicker": "Chapter 5", "title": "The map", "text": "Here is the whole record, five and a half years, against QQQ itself. The gray line is the index. The amber line is us. Twenty twenty-one opened with seven weeks of waiting. The gates never turned green, so the strategy sat in cash while the market climbed without it. February twenty-fifth: the first qualifying entry. The bull ran all year, and on December seventh, the rules banked thirteen thousand dollars in profit, weeks before the market peaked. Then came twenty twenty-two. The regime filter said bear, and the strategy went to cash for a full year, while QQQ fell thirty-five percent from its high. Sitting out felt like missing out. It was the most valuable decision of the five years. April twenty twenty-three: re-entry. That autumn brought our worst hole, seventeen point eight percent, peak to trough. Leverage cuts both ways. Then two years of patient compounding. And the final cycle: the September twenty twenty-five entry you heard about, the March twenty twenty-six correction, the June roll that banked twenty-six thousand dollars. The final mark: one hundred sixty-nine thousand, two hundred forty-nine dollars, against seventy thousand, nine hundred for simply holding QQQ. Every moment you just saw is in the ledger.", "audio": "/audio/landing/map.mp3"}, {"id": "ch4", "kicker": "Chapter 6", "title": "The drawdown", "text": "September, twenty twenty-three. The recovery is five months old, and the position is fully on. Then the autumn dip takes the portfolio from sixty-two thousand, one hundred three dollars, down to fifty-one thousand, sixty-seven. Seventeen point eight percent, lived day by day, over seven weeks. And here is what we will not hide: the model that prices the early years smooths the storms. In March twenty twenty-six, measured on the real exchange tape, the same strategy drew down thirty point four percent. Deeper than anything in the model years. Both numbers stay on this page, because both are true. The system followed its rules, and the market came back. But hear this clearly: past performance, simulated or live, does not guarantee future results. The next drawdown could be deeper. The recovery is never owed to you.", "audio": "/audio/landing/ch4.mp3"}, {"id": "ch5", "kicker": "Chapter 7", "title": "The honest comparison", "text": "Now the part most services leave out. Over these five and a half years, simply buying and holding QQQ returned one hundred thirty-six percent, with a worst hole of thirty-five point six percent. This strategy returned four hundred sixty-four percent, with a worst hole of seventeen point eight. Return per unit of turbulence, the Sharpe ratio: the index, zero point eight. The strategy, one point four eight. We won on every measure over this window, and that is exactly why you should be skeptical. Five years is one set of weather. The model-priced years flatter our smoothness. The next bear market will not look like the last one. These numbers describe one past, not any future.", "audio": "/audio/landing/ch5.mp3"}, {"id": "ch6", "kicker": "Chapter 8", "title": "Live, right now", "text": "Since August first, twenty twenty-six, this strategy runs live on a real brokerage paper account, and as of today, that includes the trend-and-premium gate you just heard about. Every decision logged daily, in public. Current state: one hundred percent cash. No qualifying entry in two weeks. That is not a malfunction, patience is the strategy. When it acts, you see it at the same time we do. Live results may be better or worse than anything simulated.", "audio": "/audio/landing/ch6.mp3"}, {"id": "ch7", "kicker": "Chapter 9", "title": "Judge for yourself", "text": "Below: every trade. Every price. Every loss. Eight hundred six fills, each one labeled by how it was priced. Judge for yourself. This page is educational material, not investment advice or a solicitation. Simulated performance, the early years model-priced, the final fifteen months verified against the real exchange tape. TradeMind never connects to your brokerage. Signals only help you enter the order yourself.", "audio": "/audio/landing/ch7.mp3"}];

